  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Linear equations, quadratics, exponents, radicals and absolute value — the algebraic core of the test.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Algebra essentials",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Quadratic formula \\( x=\\dfrac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{b^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\); difference of squares \\( a^{2}-b^{2}=(a-b)(a+b) \\). Exponents: \\( a^{m}a^{n}=a^{m+n} \\). Absolute value \\( |x|=c \\) gives \\( x=\\pm c \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "figure",
        "figure": {
          "type": "fn",
          "title": "Quadratic Parabola: Vertex, Roots & Axis of Symmetry",
          "xrange": [
            -1,
            5
          ],
          "yrange": [
            -2,
            5
          ],
          "fns": [
            {
              "fn": "x^2 - 4*x + 3",
              "color": "var(--fig-indigo-2)",
              "label": "y = x² - 4x + 3"
            }
          ],
          "points": [
            {
              "x": 2,
              "y": -1,
              "label": "Vertex (2, -1)"
            },
            {
              "x": 1,
              "y": 0,
              "label": "Root (1, 0)"
            },
            {
              "x": 3,
              "y": 0,
              "label": "Root (3, 0)"
            }
          ],
          "vlines": [
            {
              "x": 2,
              "color": "var(--fig-amber)",
              "dash": "4,3",
              "label": "Axis x = 2"
            }
          ],
          "hlines": [
            {
              "y": 0,
              "color": "var(--fig-muted)",
              "dash": "4,3",
              "label": "y = 0"
            }
          ]
        },
        "caption": {
          "en": "Graph of \\( y = x^2 - 4x + 3 \\). The vertex coordinates are given by \\( x = -b/(2a) = 2 \\) and \\( y = f(2) = -1 \\). The \\( x \\)-intercepts \\( (1,0) \\) and \\( (3,0) \\) represent the real solutions to \\( x^2 - 4x + 3 = 0 \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Quadratic formula",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{b^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
