              "en": "Difference of squares",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( (a-b)(a+b) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Exponents",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( a^{m}a^{n}=a^{m+n} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Absolute value",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( x=\\pm c \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "⚠️ Classic ACT Traps: Algebra & Quadratics",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<ul><li><strong>No Formula Sheet Provided:</strong> Unlike the SAT, the ACT provides zero reference formulas. You must memorize the Quadratic Formula \\( x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a} \\) and the vertex formula \\( x = -\\frac{b}{2a} \\).</li><li><strong>Flipping Inequality Signs:</strong> When multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, always reverse the inequality symbol: \\( -3x < 12 \\Rightarrow x > -4 \\).</li><li><strong>Vieta's Sum of Roots Shortcut:</strong> For any quadratic \\( ax^2 + bx + c = 0 \\), the sum of the solutions is \\( -b/a \\) and the product of the solutions is \\( c/a \\). When the ACT asks for 'the sum of all solutions', never solve with the quadratic formula — simply evaluate \\( -b/a \\)!</li><li><strong>Discriminant Rules:</strong> The quantity \\( \\Delta = b^2 - 4ac \\) reveals solution count: \\( \\Delta > 0 \\) (2 real roots), \\( \\Delta = 0 \\) (1 real root), \\( \\Delta < 0 \\) (2 complex/imaginary roots).</li></ul>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 2.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Solve \\( 3(x-2)=12 \\). <p>\\( x-2=4 \\):</p>\\[ x=6. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 2.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Simplify \\( \\sqrt{50} \\). \\[ \\sqrt{25\\cdot 2}=5\\sqrt{2}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "For what values of \\(x\\) is \\(|2x - 3| &lt; 7\\)?",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(-7 &lt; 2x-3 &lt; 7 \\Rightarrow -4 &lt; 2x &lt; 10 \\Rightarrow -2 &lt; x &lt; 5\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "What is the sum of the solutions of the quadratic equation \\(3x^2 - 12x - 5 = 0\\)?",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "By Vieta's formulas, for any quadratic equation \\(ax^2 + bx + c = 0\\), the sum of the roots is \\(-\\frac{b}{a}\\). Here \\(a = 3\\) and \\(b = -12\\), so the sum of the solutions is \\(-\\frac{-12}{3} = 4\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
